      "description": "Career Outcomes | Bryant University Skip to Content Top Navigation Athletics Giving News Main navigation Discover Bryant Undergraduate Graduate Professional Education Discover Bryant Undergraduate Graduate Professional Education Top Navigation Mobile Athletics Giving News Vision 2030 Vision 2030, our strategic plan, is evolving the Bryant experience. Learn How About Bryant At a Glance Mission and History Leadership and Faculty Institutional Effectiveness and Strategy Initiatives AI at Bryant Centers and Institutes Global Advisory Council Sustainability at Bryant Wellbeing at Bryant Connect Partnering With Bryant Smithfield Resources Working at Bryant Contact Us Why Bryant We transform students into leaders with the drive, vision, and experience to leave a legacy. Learn How Career Outcomes Students achieve exceptional outcomes through career planning and the Amica Center for Career Education. Explore Your Path Our unique major-minor combination is a strength that leads to endless career possibilities. Explore Your Path Campus Life Bryant’s vibrant community is a transformative place to live and learn. Explore Campus Life Clubs and Organizations With over 100 student-run clubs, Bryant has something for everyone. Athletics Experience the competitive Bryant spirit firsthand through our athletic programs. Our Campus Residential Life Student Support Services Belonging and Wellbeing at Bryant New Student Programs Women’s Leadership at Bryant Campus Map Smithfield, RI, and Beyond Academics Discover your passions through Bryant’s interdisciplinary education. Academics Overview Experiential Learning Experiential education is at the core of your Bryant experience. Learn More Our Colleges College of Business College of Health and Behavioral Sciences College of Humanities and Social Sciences Learning at Bryant Explore our labs, faculty, and academic programs. Academic Departments Academic Labs General Education Curriculum Honors Program Our Faculty View Our Programs Admission Take your first step toward becoming a Bryant Bulldog. Learn More Application Info How to Apply Tuition and Financial Aid First-Year Students International Students Transfer Students Admitted Students Admitted Class Profile Take Action Apply Now Visit Campus Request Info Take Our Virtual Tour Precollege Summer Programs Important Dates Sun, Nov 01 Early Decision I Sun, Nov 15 Early Action Mon, Feb 01 Regular Decision Academics Our graduate programs offer an interdisciplinary education that prepares students for impactful careers. Learn More Our Faculty Our dedicated faculty members offer both industry expertise and personalized mentorship. Meet Our Faculty Our Programs Explore our nationally recognized graduate programs. All Programs MBAs Online Certificates Admission Advance your career through one of our nationally recognized programs. Learn More Application Info Tuition and Financial Aid International Students Important Dates Take Action Apply Now Request Info Contact Us Graduate Blog Important Dates Wed, Jul 15 On Campus Programs: Spring 2027 Priority Deadline View All Deadlines Self-Paced Learn anytime, anywhere with flexible self-paced courses. Instructor Led Expert-led courses offer structure, support, and results. Applied AI Academy Build the skills to leverage AI effectively in your role, team, and organization. Contact an Advisor Need some advice on next steps? Connect with a Bryant Course Advisor to help. Contact an Advisor View all Certificates Home Why Bryant Career Outcomes With a transformative education that delivers exceptional outcomes, our results speak for themselves. $ 77K median starting salary of Bryant graduates Class of 2025 Top 1 % ROI for lifetime earnings Georgetown University CEW 98 % employed or in grad school within 6 months of graduation Class of 2025 98 % of graduating seniors agree that Bryant prepared them well for the future Class of 2025 190+ employers attend on-campus career events each year $ 122K mid-career salary Career Planning and Development There’s a reason employers want to hire Bryant graduates. Career planning is woven throughout your student journey. From your very first year, you’ll receive comprehensive guidance choosing your course of study, developing your career goals, and finding the right professional opportunities. At the end of your Bryant experience, we’re certain you’ll be ready for the road ahead. Here are a few ways we ensure our students achieve exceptional career outcomes. Interdisciplinary Education Model Bryant University offers you a uniquely integrated business education, helping you pave the way for your future. By complementing a business major or minor with a course of study in another discipline, our students can pursue multiple interests while also gaining a competitive advantage. Our interdisciplinary approach is a strength that gives you the expertise to solve problems from different perspectives. You’ll leave campus as a confident leader who can take on today’s biggest challenges — and stand out as an exemplary candidate as you prepare for your career. Bryant University offers you a uniquely integrated business education, helping you pave the way for your future. By complementing a business major or minor with a course of study in another discipline, our students can pursue multiple interests while also gaining a competitive advantage. Our interdisciplinary approach is a strength that gives you the expertise to solve problems from different perspectives. You’ll leave campus as a confident leader who can take on today’s biggest challenges — and stand out as an exemplary candidate as you prepare for your career. Transformative Learning Experiences Lessons from a textbook can only take you so far. The best way to understand the concepts you learn in the classroom is to apply them to real-world settings. That’s why experiential learning has always been a hallmark of the Bryant experience. Throughout your courses at Bryant — beginning your very first year — you’ll engage in internships, international learning, research opportunities, and capstone projects while partnering with real businesses and organizations. These hands-on opportunities will expose you to new ideas and elevate your leadership skills to the next level. Lessons from a textbook can only take you so far. The best way to understand the concepts you learn in the classroom is to apply them to real-world settings. That’s why experiential learning has always been a hallmark of the Bryant experience. Throughout your courses at Bryant — beginning your very first year — you’ll engage in internships, international learning, research opportunities, and capstone projects while partnering with real businesses and organizations. These hands-on opportunities will expose you to new ideas and elevate your leadership skills to the next level. Career-Ready Mindset We lead our Bulldogs to find the intersection of their passions and strengths, then equip them with the confidence and credentials to reach a fulfilling profession. This begins your first year in our “Career Launch” course, part of the general education curriculum . This class will help you solidify your career interests as you map out your course of study. You’ll create a series of action steps to help you achieve important milestones — and utilize helpful planning tools and resources — in your career development process. For undecided students who need a little more guidance, the MyPath@Bryant program in the Amica Center for Career Education provides personalized career coaching, assessments, and student mentorship to help you make an informed decision. We also help our students cultivate job search skills so they’re ready to engage with employers when the time comes. You can participate in resume reviews and mock interviews, learn how to network, get help with your LinkedIn profile, practice salary negotiation, and much more. We lead our Bulldogs to find the intersection of their passions and strengths, then equip them with the confidence and credentials to reach a fulfilling profession. This begins your first year in our “Career Launch” course, part of the general education curriculum . This class will help you solidify your career interests as you map out your course of study. You’ll create a series of action steps to help you achieve important milestones — and utilize helpful planning tools and resources — in your career development process. For undecided students who need a little more guidance, the MyPath@Bryant program in the Amica Center for Career Education provides personalized career coaching, assessments, and student mentorship to help you make an informed decision. We also help our students cultivate job search skills so they’re ready to engage with employers when the time comes. You can participate in resume reviews and mock interviews, learn how to network, get help with your LinkedIn profile, practice salary negotiation, and much more. Extensive Professional Network Over 400 employers participate in our recruitment efforts, including more than 150 employers who conduct on-campus interviews. Bryant hosts two annual on-campus career fairs featuring employers from a range of industries. We also hold networking events and site visits throughout the year to help students find internship, volunteer, and employment opportunities. And with an active alumni network of more than 50,000, there are always Bulldogs looking to connect with our current students. No matter what your discipline or career goals may be, your exposure to employers and organizations at Bryant will be unparalleled. Over 400 employers participate in our recruitment efforts, including more than 150 employers who conduct on-campus interviews. Bryant hosts two annual on-campus career fairs featuring employers from a range of industries. We also hold networking events and site visits throughout the year to help students find internship, volunteer, and employment opportunities. And with an active alumni network of more than 50,000, there are always Bulldogs looking to connect with our current students. No matter what your discipline or career goals may be, your exposure to employers and organizations at Bryant will be unparalleled. In This Section Sibling Nav Career Outcomes Explore Your Path Amica Center Our Amica Center for Career Education helps you pursue a career where you will excel. Receive personalized coaching, find job and internship opportunities, connect with employer networks, and much more. Visit the Amica Center No. 9 Best Career Services Princeton Review Experiential Learning Experiential education is at the core of your Bryant experience. Our innovative model features hands-on learning opportunities throughout the curriculum, helping you discover new insights and build analytical skills for your future. Spark Your Curiosity Explore Your Path By pursuing both a major and minor — with one in business and one in the humanities or sciences — you’ll learn how to assess problems from different perspectives and find creative solutions to today’s biggest challenges. Our interdisciplinary approach is a strength that leads to endless career possibilities. Try Our Career Widget Latest News More News Bryant rises to 9th nationally for career services, 16th best-run college in 2027 Princeton Review rankings University also earns national recognition for institutional excellence, student experience, academic resources At 163rd Commencement, Bryant’s largest-ever graduating class celebrates growth and new horizons ‘May you fail wisely, learn deeply, and contribute courageously,’ said Commencement speaker Amy Edmondson Bryant’s College of Business receives high marks for academic experience, career outcomes in 2026 Poets&Quants survey In national survey that considers student feedback, Bryant among top 15 for academic experience and top 50 for career outcomes Bryant announces direct admission partnership with MGH Institute of Health Professions Direct pathways will fuel workforce pipeline for regional healthcare sector “We're setting the pace. We're building this future”: Rupendra Paliwal, Ph.D., on reimagining higher education in the age of AI Provost and Chief Academic Officer shares Bryant University's vision of tomorrow Three ways to a Bryant MBA Bryant’s full-time, part-time, and online MBA programs offer excellent ROI, flexibility, affordability Prepared to lead: Class of 2024 earns highest starting salary in university history 99% of the class employed or pursuing advanced degrees within six months Bryant again recognized for top 1% ROI nationally by Georgetown study 20-year NPV is $1.1 million; 40-year NPV is $3 million. Bryant announces new tuition-paid internship policy, expanding experiential opportunities to enhance outcomes for all Students can now earn course credit for on- and off-semester internships In This Section Sibling Nav Career Outcomes Explore Your Path 1150 Douglas Pike, Smithfield, RI 02917 (401) 232-6000 Quick Links At a Glance Information Directory Working at Bryant Giving to Bryant Alumni Bryant News Admission Bryant Bulldogs Campus Map Career Services Events my.bryant.edu For Parents Info for Parents Pay My Bill Health Services Student Services Academic Calendar Bryant Bookstore Privacy Policy Accessibility Emergency Information ©2026 The Trustees of Bryant University. All rights reserved."
