      "description": "Amica Center for Career Education | Bryant University Skip to Content Top Navigation Athletics Giving News Main navigation Discover Bryant Undergraduate Graduate Professional Education Discover Bryant Undergraduate Graduate Professional Education Top Navigation Mobile Athletics Giving News Vision 2030 Vision 2030, our strategic plan, is evolving the Bryant experience. Learn How About Bryant At a Glance Mission and History Leadership and Faculty Institutional Effectiveness and Strategy Initiatives AI at Bryant Centers and Institutes Global Advisory Council Sustainability at Bryant Wellbeing at Bryant Connect Partnering With Bryant Smithfield Resources Working at Bryant Contact Us Why Bryant We transform students into leaders with the drive, vision, and experience to leave a legacy. Learn How Career Outcomes Students achieve exceptional outcomes through career planning and the Amica Center for Career Education. Explore Your Path Our unique major-minor combination is a strength that leads to endless career possibilities. Explore Your Path Campus Life Bryant’s vibrant community is a transformative place to live and learn. Explore Campus Life Clubs and Organizations With over 100 student-run clubs, Bryant has something for everyone. Athletics Experience the competitive Bryant spirit firsthand through our athletic programs. Our Campus Residential Life Student Support Services Belonging and Wellbeing at Bryant New Student Programs Women’s Leadership at Bryant Campus Map Smithfield, RI, and Beyond Academics Discover your passions through Bryant’s interdisciplinary education. Academics Overview Experiential Learning Experiential education is at the core of your Bryant experience. Learn More Our Colleges College of Business College of Health and Behavioral Sciences College of Humanities and Social Sciences Learning at Bryant Explore our labs, faculty, and academic programs. Academic Departments Academic Labs General Education Curriculum Honors Program Our Faculty View Our Programs Admission Take your first step toward becoming a Bryant Bulldog. Learn More Application Info How to Apply Tuition and Financial Aid First-Year Students International Students Transfer Students Admitted Students Admitted Class Profile Take Action Apply Now Visit Campus Request Info Take Our Virtual Tour Precollege Summer Programs Important Dates Sun, Nov 01 Early Decision I Sun, Nov 15 Early Action Mon, Feb 01 Regular Decision Academics Our graduate programs offer an interdisciplinary education that prepares students for impactful careers. Learn More Our Faculty Our dedicated faculty members offer both industry expertise and personalized mentorship. Meet Our Faculty Our Programs Explore our nationally recognized graduate programs. All Programs MBAs Online Certificates Admission Advance your career through one of our nationally recognized programs. Learn More Application Info Tuition and Financial Aid International Students Important Dates Take Action Apply Now Request Info Contact Us Graduate Blog Important Dates Wed, Jul 15 On Campus Programs: Spring 2027 Priority Deadline View All Deadlines Self-Paced Learn anytime, anywhere with flexible self-paced courses. Instructor Led Expert-led courses offer structure, support, and results. Applied AI Academy Build the skills to leverage AI effectively in your role, team, and organization. Contact an Advisor Need some advice on next steps? Connect with a Bryant Course Advisor to help. Contact an Advisor View all Certificates Career Development from Day One Amica Center for Career Education Your career doesn’t start after college—it begins the moment you arrive. The Amica Center connects Bryant students with internships, employers, and real-world experiences that lead to jobs after graduation. Access Handshake below. Student Login Employer Login Alumni Support Hear From Our Students From First Meeting to First Internship From exploring majors to landing your first internship, the Amica Center helps you build confidence, connections, and career direction every step of the way. Hardee Patel '27 Hardee Patel '27 Majors: Team and Project Management, Digital Marketing Minor: Communication “ “Going into my first career fair, I saw over 100 employers, all looking to hire Bryant students. I was able to explore dozens of internship opportunities, meet and talk to recruiters, and get my name out there.” Jason Ferrero '26 Jason Ferrero '26 Major: Data Science Minor: Business Administration Outcome: PL Rotational Program Analyst at the Hanover Insurance Group “ “One thing that you should know about Bryant is that we have a really strong career services center. So as for me, I came in as a finance major, but mentally I was really undecided. But after a 30 minute consultation with the career coaches in the career center, I narrowed down my major and I ended up switching from finance to data science.” Elijah Infante '25 Elijah Infante '25 Major: Politics and Law Minors: Business Administration, History and Legal Studies “ “With the help of the Amica Center for Career Education, I've been able to secure an internship with a top law firm, Hinckley, Allen and Snyder. As a legal intern, I was able to shadow real attorneys and work with other legal professionals. Seeing my work applied in real life situations allowed me to see how well prepared I am for the future.” Home Discover Bryant Centers and Institutes Your Career Starts Here At Bryant, your ambition matters. The Amica Center for Career Education helps turn your goals into real-world experience through career coaching, employer partnerships, and hands-on learning opportunities. From your first semester through graduation, you’ll build the skills employers value most — gaining experience through internships, industry engagement, and personalized advising that prepares you to launch your career with confidence. Daily Drop-In Hours Students can meet with a peer Career Advocate during daily Drop-In Hours — Monday through Friday, 11 am – 2 pm. By the Numbers 1,000+ individual 1-on-1 consultations in one semester 50% of Bryant students meet individually with a career coach by their senior year Nearly Every Student engages with the Amica Center through coaching, events, or internships 100% of Bryant students receive career development education through GEN103 Your Career Journey at Bryant At Bryant, career development unfolds as a journey of discovery , experience , focus , and launch . Students begin by exploring their interests and learning about potential career paths with support from the Amica Center. As they progress, they gain real-world experience through internships, employer engagement, and professional development opportunities. Along the way, they refine their goals, expand their networks, and strengthen the skills employers seek. By graduation, Bryant students are prepared to enter the workforce with experience, connections, and the confidence to succeed. What Bryant Students Graduate With At Bryant, career development is built into the student experience. Through internships, employer partnerships, and hands-on learning, students graduate with the skills, experience, and professional network needed to succeed from day one. Real-world experience through internships, applied learning, and industry projects Career clarity through advising, assessments, and career exploration tools Employer connections built through career fairs, networking events, and recruiting programs Professional skills including communication, interviewing, networking, and leadership A powerful professional network of alumni, faculty mentors, and industry partners And the results speak for themselves. Why Bryant’s Career Support Stands Out In a crowded field of excellent schools, Bryant’s outcomes — and the support behind them — stand apart: 98 % Bryant Graduates are employed or in graduate school within six months Top 5 Nationally for Internships LinkedIn No. 9 Career Services Princeton Review In This Section Sibling Nav Academic Center for Excellence Amica Center for Career Education Bryant University Sales Institute Center for Health and Behavioral Sciences Ellen Wilson Leadership Center Financial Markets Center John H. Chafee Center for International Business Sprague Center for Entrepreneurship and Design Thinking Stay Connected Unistructure, 1st Floor – Amica Center Phone (401) 232-6090 careers@bryant.edu Instagram Additional Resources Related Links Bryant University on Handshake EXPLORE Careers in the Cities Where They Happen Bryant’s EXPLORE Programs bring career discovery beyond campus. Students travel to industry hubs like New York City and Washington, D.C. , while rotating experiences introduce them to professional communities in Providence, Boston, Chicago, San Francisco, Miami, and Dallas —connecting them with alumni, employers, and emerging opportunities. Walk Down Wall Street Visit leading financial firms in New York City, connect with Bryant alumni on Wall Street, and gain firsthand insight into careers in finance and investment. Arts in the City Spend five days in New York City meeting alumni and professionals across film, music, publishing, fashion, theater, and other creative industries. National Retail Program A 4-day travel experience in New York hosted by National Retail Federation. EXPLORE DC Travel to Washington, D.C to learn about government, policy, & law careers. Internships and Career Prep Bryant students gain hands-on experience through internships, industry projects, and employer partnerships. The Amica Center helps you explore industries, connect with employers, and secure opportunities that launch your career. Internships and Career Prep Experiential Learning Real-world experience is a Bryant hallmark. Whether you pursue internships for credit or not, our advisors help you evaluate roles, prepare strong applications, and succeed on the job. Bryant’s internship policy allows students to complete internships for credit at no additional tuition cost. This along with the Summer Internship Fellowship for unpaid or low-paid experiences, ensures you have access to opportunities that accelerate your growth. Learn More Career Development Program The Amica Center’s Career Development Program supports students at every stage of the Bryant Career Journey , helping them build the skills, experience, and professional confidence employers expect. Through workshops, coaching, employer engagement, and hands-on opportunities, students develop the tools they need to explore careers, secure internships, and launch successful professional paths. Read about Career Launch Employer Partnerships & Recruiting Employers know Bryant graduates are ready to contribute on day one. Through career fairs, industry nights, classroom engagement, and company site visits, you’ll meet organizations actively looking for talent. Handshake gives you direct access to tens of thousands of jobs and internships across industries and regions. Become a Partner Employer Login (Handshake) Accessible Resources — Anytime, Anywhere Students have access to digital tools like Handshake for internships, job postings, and employer events — plus resume resources, interview prep, and industry research. Career Resource Hub Pathways to Success Students, employers, and alumni each play a vital role in Bryant’s career ecosystem. Explore the pathway that best supports your goals, and discover what’s possible with the Amica Center behind you. Internships and Career Prep From your first year at Bryant, you’re not just imagining your future — you’re actively building it. The Amica Center helps you discover what you’re good at, test-drive industries through internships, and graduate with the skills, experience, and network employers value most. Employers Hire Bryant Talent Bryant students bring analytical rigor, communication strength, and real-world experience across business, liberal arts, health and behavioral sciences, and technology. Our employer relations team makes it easy to connect with this talent — through fairs, events, recruiting programs, and direct outreach. Alumni & the Amica Center As your career grows, so does your connection to Bryant. The Amica Center and Alumni & Parent Engagement team offer early-career support, networking opportunities, and avenues to mentor and hire emerging talent — helping you lead with confidence while strengthening the Bulldog community. Meet the Team You won’t be navigating this journey alone. The Amica Center team includes experienced career coaches, employer-relations professionals, and experiential education specialists who know how to connect Bryant talent with opportunity. Veronica Stewart Director Ashley Larson Office Coordinator Nicole Potvin Senior Assistant Director of Career Services Michael Wisnewski Senior Career Coach Erin Cheschi Senior Career Coach Melanie Ok Intercultural Career Coach Amy Steere Assistant Director of Experiential Education Katie Taylor Experiential Education Coordinator Pat Miernicki Associate Director of Employer Relations Scott Connolly Senior Assistant Director, Employer Relations Latest News More News Bryant rises to 9th nationally for career services, 16th best-run college in 2027 Princeton Review rankings University also earns national recognition for institutional excellence, student experience, academic resources Co-op programs give students extended experience in the workplace Six-month, full-time stints with employers offer undergrads more responsibility and leadership opportunities Bryant, Fidelity partnership is a pipeline to success Internships and a new co-op program launch finance careers for Bryant students ‘We are going to bring each other up’: Women in Finance mentorship fosters connection, opportunity Julia Di Natale ’22 and Molly Stokes ’28 forge lasting bond through mentorship initiative Bryant’s Women in Finance get inside tours of Red Bull, Chicago Blackhawks, and more Three-day Chicago trip includes meetings with alumni, diverse companies, and successful businesswomen At 163rd Commencement, Bryant’s largest-ever graduating class celebrates growth and new horizons ‘May you fail wisely, learn deeply, and contribute courageously,’ said Commencement speaker Amy Edmondson After farming and cheesemaking, Glenn Diana Sherman '26MBA cultivates a new career path Business skills will complement passion for local food, community organizing, she says Amazon’s ‘Last Mile’ operations are a big first step for Karina Escobar ’26 GCSM major helps manage a team that ships 100,000 packages daily From bias incident research to advocacy-focused internships, Bryant senior prepares for a career in forensic psychology ‘It's going to work out as long as you show up, put the work in, and do your best,’ says Maya Niemeyer ’26 In This Section Sibling Nav Academic Center for Excellence Amica Center for Career Education Bryant University Sales Institute Center for Health and Behavioral Sciences Ellen Wilson Leadership Center Financial Markets Center John H. Chafee Center for International Business Sprague Center for Entrepreneurship and Design Thinking Stay Connected Unistructure, 1st Floor – Amica Center Phone (401) 232-6090 careers@bryant.edu Instagram Additional Resources Related Links Bryant University on Handshake Take Action Visit Get a firsthand look at life as a Bryant student. Register Virtual Tour Apply Find everything you need to guide you through the admission process. Apply Request Info 1150 Douglas Pike, Smithfield, RI 02917 (401) 232-6000 Quick Links At a Glance Information Directory Working at Bryant Giving to Bryant Alumni Bryant News Admission Bryant Bulldogs Campus Map Career Services Events my.bryant.edu For Parents Info for Parents Pay My Bill Health Services Student Services Academic Calendar Bryant Bookstore Privacy Policy Accessibility Emergency Information ©2026 The Trustees of Bryant University. All rights reserved."
