on Sibling Nav Academic Center for Excellence Amica Center for Career Education Bryant University Sales Institute Center for Health and Behavioral Sciences Ellen Wilson Leadership Center Financial Markets Center John H. Chafee Center for International Business Sprague Center for Entrepreneurship and Design Thinking Stay Connected Unistructure, 1st Floor – Amica Center Phone (401) 232-6090 careers@bryant.edu Instagram Additional Resources Related Links Bryant University on Handshake EXPLORE Careers in the Cities Where They Happen Bryant’s EXPLORE Programs bring career discovery beyond campus. Students travel to industry hubs like New York City and Washington, D.C. , while rotating experiences introduce them to professional communities in Providence, Boston, Chicago, San Francisco, Miami, and Dallas —connecting them with alumni, employers, and emerging opportunities. Walk Down Wall Street Visit leading financial firms in New York City, connect with Bryant alumni on Wall Street, and gain firsthand insight into careers in finance and investment. Arts in the City Spend five days in New York City meeting alumni and professionals across film, music, publishing, fashion, theater, and other creative industries. National Retail Program A 4-day travel experience in New York hosted by National Retail Federation. EXPLORE DC Travel to Washington, D.C to learn about government, policy, & law careers. Internships and Career Prep Bryant students gain hands-on experience through internships, industry projects, and employer partnerships. The Amica Center helps you explore industries, connect with employers, and secure opportunities that launch your career. Internships and Career Prep Experiential Learning Real-world experience is a Bryant hallmark. Whether you pursue internships for credit or not, our advisors help you evaluate roles, prepare strong applications, and succeed on the job. Bryant’s internship policy allows students to complete internships for credit at no additional tuition cost. This along with the Summer Internship Fellowship for unpaid or low-paid experiences, ensures you have access to opportunities that accelerate your growth. Learn More Career Development Program The Amica Center’s Career Development Program supports students at every stage of the Bryant Career Journey , helping them build the skills, experience, and professional confidence employers expect. Through workshops, coaching, employer engagement, and hands-on opportunities, students develop the tools they need to explore careers, secure internships, and launch successful professional paths. Read about Career Launch Employer Partnerships & Recruiting Employers know Bryant graduates are ready to contribute on day one. Through career fairs, industry nights, classroom engagement, and company site visits, you’ll meet organizations actively looking for talent. Handshake gives you direct access to tens of thousands of jobs and internships across industries and regions. Become a Partner Employer Login (Handshake) Accessible Resources — Anytime, Anywhere Students have access to digital tools like Handshake for internships, job postings, and employer events — plus resume resources, interview prep, and industry research. Career Resource Hub Pathways to Success Students, employers, and alumni each play a vital role in Bryant’s career ecosystem. Explore the pathway that best supports your goals, and discover what’s possible with the Amica Center behind you. Internships and Career Prep From your first year at Bryant, you’re not just imagining your future — you’re actively building it. The Amica Center helps you discover what you’re good at, test-drive industries through internships, and graduate with the skills, experience, and network employers value most. Employers Hire Bryant Talent Bryant students bring analytical rigor, communication strength, and real-world experience across business, liberal arts, health and behavioral sciences, and technology. Our employer relations team makes it easy to connect with this talent — through fairs, events, recruiting programs, and direct outreach. Alumni & the Amica Center As your career grows, so does your connection to Bryant. The Amica Center and Alumni & Parent Engagement team offer early-career support, networking opportunities, and avenues to mentor and hire emerging talent — helping you lead with confidence while strengthening the Bulldog community. Meet the Team You won’t be navigating this journey alone. The Amica Center team includes experienced career coaches, employer-relations professionals, and experiential education specialists who know how to connect Bryant talent with opportunity. Veronica Stewart Director Ashley Larson Office Coordinator Nicole Potvin Senior Assistant Director of Career Services Michael Wisnewski Senior Career Coach Erin Cheschi Senior Career Coach Melanie Ok Intercultural Career Coach Amy Steere Assistant Director of Experiential Education Katie Taylor Experiential Education Coordinator Pat Miernicki Associate Director of Employer Relations Scott Connolly Senior Assistant Director, Employer Relations Latest News More News Bryant rises to 9th nationally for career services, 16th best-run college in 2027 Princeton Review rankings University also earns national recognition for institutional excellence, student experience, academic resources Co-op programs give students extended experience in the workplace Six-month, full-time stints with employers offer undergrads more responsibility and leadership opportunities Bryant, Fidelity partnership is a pipeline to success Internships and a new co-op program launch finance careers for Bryant students ‘We are going to bring each other up’: Women in Finance mentorship fosters connection, opportunity Julia Di Natale ’22 and Molly Stokes ’28 forge lasting bond through mentorship initiative Bryant’s Women in Finance get inside tours of Red Bull, Chicago Blackhawks, and more Three-day Chicago trip includes meetings with alumni, diverse companies, and successful businesswomen At 163rd Commencement, Bryant’s largest-ever graduating class celebrates growth and new horizons ‘May you fail wisely, learn deeply, and contribute courageously,’ said Commencement speaker Amy Edmondson After farming and cheesemaking, Glenn Diana Sherman '26MBA cultivates a new career path Business skills will complement passion for local food, community organizing, she says Amazon’s ‘Last Mile’ operations are a big first step for Karina Escobar ’26 GCSM major helps manage a team that ships 100,000 packages daily From bias incident research to advocacy-focused internships, Bryant senior prepares for a career in forensic psychology ‘It's going to work out as long as you show up, put the work in, and do your best,’ says Maya Niemeyer ’26 In This Section Sibling Nav Academic Center for Excellence Amica Center for Career Education Bryant University Sales Institute Center for Health and Behavioral Sciences Ellen Wilson Leadership Center Financial Markets Center John H. Chafee Center for International Business Sprague Center for Entrepreneurship and Design Thinking Stay Connected Unistructure, 1st Floor – Amica Center Phone (401) 232-6090 careers@bryant.edu Instagram Additional Resources Related Links Bryant University on Handshake Take Action Visit Get a firsthand look at life as a Bryant student. Register Virtual Tour Apply Find everything you need to guide you through the admission process. Apply Request Info 1150 Douglas Pike, Smithfield, RI 02917 (401) 232-6000 Quick Links At a Glance Information Directory Working at Bryant Giving to Bryant Alumni Bryant News Admission Bryant Bulldogs Campus Map Career Services Events my.bryant.edu For Parents Info for Parents Pay My Bill Health Services Student Services Academic Calendar Bryant Bookstore Privacy Policy Accessibility Emergency Information ©2026 The Trustees of Bryant University. All rights reserved."
